<title>PERU: Peru's September silver output falls 3.4 percent.</title>
<headline>Peru's September silver output falls 3.4 percent.</headline>
<dateline>LIMA 1996-10-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Peru's silver output fell 3.4 percent to 159,590 tonnes in September, compared with the same month last year, according to preliminary figures from the Energy and Mines Ministry released Tuesday.</p>
<p>Production rose 2.7 percent to 1.444 million tonnes in the first nine months of the year, compared with the same period last year, the ministry said.</p>
<p>Peru is the world's number two silver producer after Mexico.</p>
<p>State-owned mining company Centromin Peru is the country's largest producer.</p>
<p>-- Saul Hudson, Lima newsroom 511 221-2134</p>
